  "architectural_summary": "**Architectural Summary: Slidev**\n\n**1. Overall Architecture Pattern:**  \nSlidev is a **monolithic, static-site generator** built as a Node.js CLI tool and dev server. It follows a **plugin-based architecture** (visible in `docs/custom/` config files) where core functionality is extended via add-ons, themes, and Vite/Unocss integrations.\n\n**2. Tech Stack:**  \n- **Frontend:** Vue 3 (Composition API), Vite (build tool), UnoCSS (utility-first CSS), Shiki (syntax highlighting), Monaco Editor (embedded IDE).  \n- **Testing:** Cypress for E2E (`cypress/e2e/`), Vitest likely for unit tests.  \n- **Docs:** Static site (likely Vitepress) under `docs/`.  \n\n**3. API Surface:**  \nNo traditional backend API; instead, a **CLI-driven interface** (`slidev` commands) and **development server** with hot-reload. The \"API\" is the slide deck definition via Markdown files with frontmatter and Vue components.\n\n**4. Data Layer:**  \nNo persistent database. Data models are **slide definitions** (Markdown with YAML frontmatter) and **theme/addon configurations**. The project uses file-based storage for assets and slide content.\n\n**5. Infrastructure Maturity:**  \n- **CI/CD:** GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/` for testing, releases, and smoke tests).  \n- **Deployment:** Static hosting (Netlify config `netlify.toml`).  \n- **Containerization:** None evident; tool is distributed as an NPM package.  \n\n**6. Strengths:**  \n- **Modular and extensible:** Clear separation of core, themes (`docs/guide/write-theme.md`), and add-ons.  \n- **Developer experience:** Integrated editor, live preview, and rich demo suite (`demo/`).  \n- **Testing:** Robust E2E coverage with Cypress, including example decks.  \n\n**7. Weaknesses / Gaps:**  \n- **No containerization:** Limits reproducibility in diverse environments.  \n- **Monolithic CLI:** Could benefit from lighter, composable modules (e.g., separate renderer/editor).  \n- **Documentation complexity:** Extensive config options (`docs/custom/`) may overwhelm new users.  \n- **Lack of backend services:** Advanced features (collaboration, analytics) would require external integration.  \n\n**Overall:** Slidev is a well-architected, developer-focused tool for technical presentations, leveraging modern Vue/Vite ecosystems. Its static nature simplifies deployment but limits real-time features.",
